date:        Wed, 09 Sep 2026 11:07:19 -0700

    Tighten WebTransport StreamReadHandle lifetime

    A handler that closes the session or aborts the transaction from
    onWebTransport{Uni,Bidi}Stream destroys the handle that call just created, and
    HQSession::deliverWTStream registered it with quic anyway. deliverWTStream now
    holds a DestructorGuard across the callback, the transaction returns no handle
    once the handler has ended it, and a handle the handler stopped reading is left
    unregistered; stopReadingWebTransportIngress falls back to
    QuicSocket::stopSending so a stopSending() from the new-stream callback still
    sends STOP_SENDING.

    terminateSessionStreams only unregistered the read callback for open() handles,
    so a handle that saw a FIN with no read outstanding was destroyed while quic
    still held it. Handles now track registration and every one we destroy is
    unregistered. Finally, deliverPendingWTStreams re-resolves the CONNECT stream
    each iteration, since delivering one buffered stream can destroy it.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

